    {
      "id": "CVE-2026-114508",
      "aliases": [
        "GHSA-5wcm-3v2w-8362"
      ],
      "title": "Laravel relationship inclusion can trigger unauthorized data destruction",
      "summary": "Laravel is a web application framework. From 12.45.0 until 12.68.0 and 13.27.0, crafted relationship inclusion on a read-only endpoint can trigger a destructive database operation on a related table instead of retrieving data. A user with read access but no write permission can empty related-table data, causing irreversible data loss, denial of service, and loss of data integrity. This issue is fixed in versions 12.68.0 and 13.27.0.",
